**Business Overview: Satellite and Space Systems Division**

**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Prepared by:** AstraTech Innovations, Inc.  
**Location:** Cape Canaveral, Florida  

AstraTech Innovations, Inc. continues to lead the development of advanced satellite and rocket systems to support both commercial and defense sectors. Our collaboration with key defense contractors, including Lockheed Martin and Northrop Grumman, has enabled us to enhance our satellite capabilities, particularly in the area of secure communication systems. The recent launch of our Titan-9 rocket on September 30, 2023, successfully deployed the Sentinel-3 Earth observation satellite into low Earth orbit, marking a significant milestone in our Earth monitoring initiative.

Our partnerships with NASA and the United States Department of Defense (DoD) are pivotal to our research and development efforts, ensuring that our systems meet stringent operational standards. The Titan-9 rocket is designed using cutting-edge technology from our R&D team, which includes experts like Dr. Emily Carter and Dr. Raj Patel, who have contributed significantly to propulsion systems and materials science.

